Z||000000||Phaeton||02-15-2000||03:39 AM||||I was driving down Airport Road coming up on Alaskaland, big local tourist trap, wide entrance, large parking lot.  It's the offseason but the waterhose for the motorhomes is still turned on, I have two 6 gallon jugs in the trunk, and its right on my way.<BR>I put the Fiero in second gear and hold 3000 right up to the entrance then twist Hard on the wheel and goose it, trying for a 90 degree turn.  Right in front of me is a minuture white station wagon with a four year old boy in the passenger seat with his mom's arm flung across his chest.  Her other arm is holding her off the steering wheel cause the brakes are locked.  I take my foot completely off the gas and keep spinning the wheel back away from the turn.  The Fiero is a dream, it whips its butt right around and I slide past with the tail starting to pass the nose.  I stop and get out to meet the miniwagon's owner.<BR>She tears me up and I say I'm sorry.<BR>She talks about her son and I say I'll look next time.<BR>She talks of fear and I say I didn't mean to.<BR>I wanted to tell her not to think of this every time she see's a small sports car.<BR>But she will.<BR>I also have small children.||||reg||11
Z||000001||Shiner||02-15-2000||05:18 AM||||I used to do this kind of stuff all the time (still do, heh)  I remember one time I was at a local flea market.  The parking lot is all grass and gravel.  I pull out, and do the exact same thing as you, fling the ass end around and pull a nice 90* turn.  This chinese guy in a minivan almost had a heart attack!  Seems like most people, when confronted with what they percive to be a danger on the road, immedietly lock up the brakes and just act scared!  ||||reg||7
